# Skill files are read by Claude Code straight from the working tree (through the
# junctions ~/.claude/skills/glm and ~/.claude/skills/agy), and its frontmatter
# parser does not accept CRLF:
# with CRLF the skill's description is lost and the H1 is shown instead, which
# breaks skill triggering. core.autocrlf=true on this machine would check the file
# out as CRLF, so pin it to LF here. Found 2026-09-15.
.claude/skills/** text eol=lf
